
-- phonelink:panel:begin
-- The reply panel is a transient prompt, not a window you work in. Tiled it
-- claims a whole column and leaves most of it empty, so float and centre it.
--
-- Deliberately no size here: phonelink asks foot for a height that fits the
-- conversation it is about to show, and a size rule would override that,
-- either clipping a group thread or leaving a one-line chat mostly empty.
--
-- Fully opaque: Omarchy's default translucency lets whatever is behind show
-- straight through an unblurred floating window, and you cannot read a message
-- with someone else's terminal underneath it.
o.window("^(org\\.omarchy\\.phonelink)$", {
  float = true,
  center = true,
  tag = "-default-opacity",
  opacity = "1 1",
})
-- phonelink:panel:end
